WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:02.502
- Try to make the best decision

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.336
as a human,

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.588
not just for yourself or selfish reasons,

00:00:05.588 --> 00:00:07.090
just for humanity.

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:11.052
- One vote might seem as
insignificant, but it is important.

00:00:11.052 --> 00:00:12.929
- Understand that, in
numbers, we have strength.

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:14.889
- Everybody needs to understand
that their vote matters.

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:17.642
- I'm JR Smith, and I'm
voting cuz my voice matters.

00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:19.561
- I'm Udonis Haslem, and I'm voting

00:00:19.561 --> 00:00:20.520
because the power is in the people.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.521
- I'm Cody Zeller,

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:22.355
and I am voting

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.274
because it's my right as a U.S. citizen.

00:00:24.274 --> 00:00:25.400
- I'm Miles Bridges,

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.111
and I am voting because my life matters.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.489
- Voting’s important to me

00:00:31.489 --> 00:00:34.117
because just so many peoples sacrificed

00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:37.120
over the course of time of our ancestors.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:42.125
So many people didn't
have the right to vote.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.836
Just to be able to say I did something,

00:00:45.837 --> 00:00:47.672
and that my opinion and my voice matters.

00:00:47.672 --> 00:00:51.634
- When you look at any of
these individual issues

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.720
in communities, whether it's Jacob Blake

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.264
or for George Floyd or Breonna Taylor,

00:00:56.264 --> 00:00:58.641
what's clear is that the decisions

00:00:58.641 --> 00:01:01.603
about what happens in local
communities usually sit

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:03.229
in the hands of elected officials,

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.856
whether it's the district attorney

00:01:04.856 --> 00:01:07.150
or the judge or the sheriff.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.360
We get the leadership that we choose.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.571
- Being from Florida and
understanding the importance

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.531
of the state of Florida,
you know, in the process,

00:01:13.531 --> 00:01:15.075
as soon as I got home,

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.701
I wanted to make it a
priority to get right

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:19.287
to the polls right there and vote.

00:01:19.287 --> 00:01:20.747
Because those are the things
that we've been pushing

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:21.581
while we were in the bubble,

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:22.916
so I wanted to make sure
we keep that momentum

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.042
when we get outside of the bubble,

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:26.503
and Florida has a lot to do

00:01:26.503 --> 00:01:28.963
with the outcome of the voting situation.

00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:30.048
Let's just say that.

00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:32.175
- One of the things that
makes our country unique

00:01:32.175 --> 00:01:33.510
compared to other countries is that

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:36.513
we do have a say in who
our leaders are gonna be.

00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:39.641
And, you know, one vote
might seem as insignificant,

00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:42.268
but it is important for everyone to vote.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.020
As I hear about some of the policies,

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.438
it really affects my life.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.065
It's not just picking between

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:49.025
which two people are my favorite.

00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:51.945
My dad has had open-heart 
surgery when I was in high school,

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:55.698
so he has an aortic valve and
a pre-existing condition.

00:01:55.698 --> 00:01:57.700
So that's one of the hot topics

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.410
for me and my family is making sure

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:02.956
that he's able to get health insurance.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.666
- The country, we're going
through a lot right now.

00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:09.254
So it's important for
everybody to get out and vote.

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:10.547
Everybody just needs to understand

00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:11.589
that their vote matters.

00:02:11.589 --> 00:02:13.216
- Do your due diligence, honestly.

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:16.636
Just do your research, take the time,

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:17.762
take this very serious.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.057
It's not something you
can just, you know, walk in

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:22.225
and breeze through.

00:02:22.225 --> 00:02:23.935
You have more candidates

00:02:23.935 --> 00:02:26.813
than just the Democrat and Republican options

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.606
that they're giving you.

00:02:28.606 --> 00:02:31.234
It takes time and consideration

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:32.652
cuz it affects a lot of people.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:33.611
It affects all of us.

00:02:33.611 --> 00:02:35.822
- Understand that in
numbers, we have strength.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.532
In numbers we have strength, people.

00:02:37.532 --> 00:02:39.951
So, it's gonna be hard.

00:02:39.951 --> 00:02:43.830
You know, we're getting
misinformation and confusion,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.081
but we have strength in numbers.

00:02:45.081 --> 00:02:48.001
- [Smith:] I was asking guys who's
voted, who's listed,

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.335
making sure guys are registered.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:50.295
At the end of the day,

00:02:50.295 --> 00:02:51.838
that's where it starts happening.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:53.339
Encouraging people in my community,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.049
my friends, my family,

00:02:55.049 --> 00:02:57.385
making sure it's starting right there,

00:02:57.385 --> 00:02:59.888
and then hopefully they
can pass that along

00:02:59.888 --> 00:03:00.847
to somebody else.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.433
- My role in the PA is
working with the players

00:03:03.433 --> 00:03:05.518
on their philanthropy
and their social impact,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:10.064
and a big part of that
is civic engagement.

00:03:10.064 --> 00:03:11.649
I don't think that we were surprised

00:03:11.649 --> 00:03:15.445
to find out that not all of
our players were registered.

00:03:15.445 --> 00:03:19.616
I think it was somewhat what we expected.

00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:20.658
No matter what you do

00:03:20.658 --> 00:03:23.203
as it relates to registering
for people to vote,

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:26.080
it's one man, one vote, one player,

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.001
one registration, and we sorta
methodically began doing that

00:03:30.001 --> 00:03:31.628
about this time last year.

00:03:31.628 --> 00:03:33.630
- [Bridges:] I would say who
helped me get out and vote

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.298
were my teammates.

00:03:35.298 --> 00:03:37.133
They're very on that.

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:40.178
My coach, he's done a great
job getting everybody to vote.

00:03:40.178 --> 00:03:43.723
He's very involved with our
Swarm to the Polls voting.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:47.143
- He's been great
throughout the whole summer,

00:03:47.143 --> 00:03:49.270
making it a big point to vote,

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:53.900
and especially get the young
guys registered and educated.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.153
He really preaches to us
to be a complete person,

00:03:57.153 --> 00:03:59.530
not just a good basketball player.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:00.657
- They were a big help.

00:04:00.657 --> 00:04:01.491
Michele Roberts,

00:04:01.491 --> 00:04:02.909
she knew to talk the talk

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.118
when it came

00:04:04.118 --> 00:04:07.914
to talking to the mayor's
office and the mayor.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:12.919
It was just very, very
inspiring to have the backing

00:04:13.002 --> 00:04:15.213
of the Players Association
more than anything.

00:04:15.213 --> 00:04:18.216
- The way we think about
arenas are gathering places

00:04:18.216 --> 00:04:20.677
for a lot of us, or for
all of us, actually.

00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:23.012
They're anchors in a
lot of the neighborhoods

00:04:23.012 --> 00:04:26.641
and communities, and
specifically for JR,

00:04:26.641 --> 00:04:28.977
even though the Prudential
Center is no longer a place

00:04:28.977 --> 00:04:30.270
where basketball is being played,

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.146
it sits right at the center of Newark.

00:04:32.146 --> 00:04:36.401
It's a part of his
experience living in Newark.

00:04:36.401 --> 00:04:39.988
And he knew that providing it
as a safe, accessible place

00:04:39.988 --> 00:04:43.157
for people to come vote was important,

00:04:43.157 --> 00:04:46.035
and he wanted to make
sure that his neighbors

00:04:46.035 --> 00:04:48.162
and family members

00:04:48.162 --> 00:04:50.623
and community could have that safe place.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.500
- Me being 40 years old now,

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.294
I'm really starting to really understand

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:56.004
all the different ways
of voter suppression

00:04:56.004 --> 00:04:57.088
and systematic racism.

00:04:57.088 --> 00:05:00.383
And for me, I was
largely voter suppressed,

00:05:00.383 --> 00:05:01.217
you know what I'm saying?

00:05:01.217 --> 00:05:02.385
I didn't think my vote even mattered.

00:05:02.385 --> 00:05:05.221
You're not having voters’
conversations with your friends.

00:05:05.221 --> 00:05:08.182
You're not being educated
on voting in school.

00:05:08.182 --> 00:05:10.143
And then when you do
get old enough to vote,

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:12.228
how do you pick somebody
that you vote for?

00:05:12.228 --> 00:05:13.104
How are you comfortable

00:05:13.104 --> 00:05:15.481
with the person that you're endorsing?

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:16.858
Those are some of the things that,

00:05:16.858 --> 00:05:18.192
you know, I wasn't even aware of,

00:05:18.192 --> 00:05:20.028
that I had to educate myself on.

00:05:20.028 --> 00:05:21.321
So now that I have this platform,

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:23.364
it's time for me to pass
that information along.

00:05:23.364 --> 00:05:24.198
- At the end of the day,

00:05:24.198 --> 00:05:25.658
I'm bigger than a basketball player.

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:26.701
So I can honestly say

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:27.785
I didn't take it as serious

00:05:27.785 --> 00:05:30.163
or look at it like that
as I did in the past,

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:32.540
but obviously everybody matures

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.458
at their own pace,

00:05:33.458 --> 00:05:36.919
so I'm just happy I'm
on the right side of it.

00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:37.754
- Everybody has a voice.

00:05:37.754 --> 00:05:39.339
No matter if you play basketball,

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:40.965
you still have a voice.

00:05:40.965 --> 00:05:42.258
And just because you play basketball,

00:05:42.258 --> 00:05:45.219
you can't just limit somebody
to just one thing in life.

00:05:45.219 --> 00:05:47.305
I feel like LeBron James, Carmelo Anthony,

00:05:47.305 --> 00:05:48.431
Chris Paul and all those guys,

00:05:48.431 --> 00:05:49.432
they've done a great job

00:05:49.432 --> 00:05:51.476
of setting the standard
for us younger guys.

00:05:51.476 --> 00:05:53.895
And we see guys like Malcolm Brogdon

00:05:53.895 --> 00:05:56.814
and Jaylen Brown,
they've definitely taken the torch.

00:05:56.814 --> 00:05:58.316
So we just wanna follow after those guys.

00:05:58.316 --> 00:05:59.442
- People are gonna look back,

00:05:59.442 --> 00:06:01.235
our kids are gonna look
back at this and say,

00:06:01.235 --> 00:06:02.820
"You were a part of that."

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:05.156
I got a grandfather that
marched next to Dr. King

00:06:05.156 --> 00:06:07.533
in the '60s, and he was amazing.

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:09.660
He would be proud to see us all here.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:11.287
We gotta keep pushing forward.

00:06:11.287 --> 00:06:12.830
- What gives me hope is
just everybody is starting

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.457
to get involved now.

00:06:14.457 --> 00:06:16.876
Before, it would only be,
like, a certain amount of guys

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:19.253
that would speak out about
it on Twitter or Instagram,

00:06:19.253 --> 00:06:22.173
but now I feel like guys
have taken to the streets.

00:06:22.173 --> 00:06:23.841
- I mean, I think it's great to see.

00:06:23.841 --> 00:06:25.760
You see the change coming.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.637
You feel the inspiration

00:06:28.679 --> 00:06:30.390
within so many young people

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:33.101
who have voices and know they have voices

00:06:33.101 --> 00:06:35.228
and know that their voice means something.

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:36.896
I think social networking alone

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:40.691
has just been so connecting

00:06:40.691 --> 00:06:43.653
to everybody, to where
we actually feel the pain

00:06:43.653 --> 00:06:45.238
and hurt that so many people go through.

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:48.241
It's not just one city

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:50.993
or one small town or one small community.

00:06:50.993 --> 00:06:53.704
It's a whole world out here where

00:06:53.704 --> 00:06:55.873
a lot of people feel the exact same way.

00:06:55.873 --> 00:06:58.543
- Unified, collectively, in numbers,

00:06:58.543 --> 00:07:00.294
bringing everybody together.

00:07:00.294 --> 00:07:01.546
It's been proven.

00:07:01.546 --> 00:07:03.965
It's been shown that, you know, we can do it

00:07:03.965 --> 00:07:04.966
if we all do it together.

00:07:04.966 --> 00:07:07.844
So, that's the most
encouraging thing to me,

00:07:07.844 --> 00:07:09.720
watching everybody come
together in the bubble.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.722
You know, that's the first time, and I've
been in this league 17 years,

00:07:11.722 --> 00:07:13.850
that I've watched everybody collectively,

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:16.477
on one platform, use their
voice for the same common goal.

00:07:16.477 --> 00:07:18.020
And that was amazing for me to see.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:18.855
- You know, one of the things

00:07:18.855 --> 00:07:20.690
I've found really interesting is

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:23.901
how excited the first-time
voters are, right?

00:07:23.901 --> 00:07:26.362
That they're able to
sort of step out there,

00:07:26.362 --> 00:07:28.531
and not just step out there
on their own and vote,

00:07:28.531 --> 00:07:30.116
but take their colleagues with them,

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:31.993
take their family members with them.

00:07:33.327 --> 00:07:35.246
I think what we have done

00:07:35.246 --> 00:07:38.040
in our league is make voting a part

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.293
of what it means to be an NBA player.

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:43.254
And I think every rookie
that walks into this league

00:07:43.254 --> 00:07:44.755
at the draft will know

00:07:44.755 --> 00:07:46.841
that even though the
election is behind us,

00:07:46.841 --> 00:07:49.677
that they'll need to register
too, and I'm proud of that.

